The total circumference is the sum of the circumferences of each individual circle:

\[
C_{\text{total}} = 2\pi(5 + 10 + 15 + 20)\;\text{m}
                 = 2\pi(50)\;\text{m}
                 = 100\pi\;\text{m}
\]

So the combined circumference is **\(100\pi \approx 314.16\) m**.
